<title>GERMANY: Polish rapeseed crop seen at 600,000-650,000 T.</title>
<headline>Polish rapeseed crop seen at 600,000-650,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's rapeseed crop in 1997 is estimated at 600,000-650,000 tonnes after 450,000 tonnes in 1996, grain trader Alfred C Toepfer's monthly newsletter said.</p>
<p>The area for 1997 was only slightly expanded to 300,000 hectares, it said, without offering a 1996 figure.</p>
<p>Toepfer put the 1995 area at 605,000 ha and the crop at 1.4 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Poland's Central Statistical Office (GUS) on Dec 17 put the 1996 acreage at 278,000 ha and the 1996 crop at 500,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>Toepfer said Poland may import up to 300,000 tonnes of rapeseed in the 1996-97 marketing year after it was able to export 400,000 tonnes from the large 1995-96 crop.</p>
</text>
